 "strings": {
  "Did I ever say the jacket was in the bag?": "",
  "Uh... Yes?": "",
  "Oh. Okay. Maybe I did say that.": "",
  "Don't come at me with this senile shit, bro.": "",
  "(Wow, I'm losing it. I better think again.)": "",
  "I didn't say anything about the bag's color, did I?": "",
  "(...Suspicious. Is there anything else I can use as ammo against these guys?)": "",
  "(Maybe one of them is wearing something they stole...)": "",
  "Hey, could I ask you a favor?": "",
  "Hm, what's the matter Yagami-san?": "",
  "Yeah, it's no problem. I have some warm stuff in my backup, so you can give him this.": "",
  "Of course. Anything for you, Yagami-san.": "",
  "Wow, thanks! I think this'll be perfect!": "",
  "(That was a huge help! I'm sure he'll go for this jacket...)": "",
  "I'm really curious what you did to get it back, but... I won't ask.": "",
  "You there. You've got one hell of a swing, you know that?": "",
  "Thanks. And you are?": "",
  "Bet a guy like you could use a <font_kind=yakuza_italic>real</font_kind> batting challenge, the likes of which no one's ever seen. Am I right?": "",
  "Well, I did clear all the previous ones like it was nobody's business.": "",
  "Indeed. Then, if you truly are the chosen one, perhaps— No... Forgive me. I've said too much already.": "",
  "Just say it.": "",
  "So be it... You see, in my darkest, loneliest hour, I devised a forbidden course for fiends with otherworldly talent... such as yourself.": "",
  "Problem is, I made it so difficult, no one could get in even a single hit! So I sealed it off from the rest of the world.": "",
  "You... sealed it off?": "",
  "Yes... It was once known as... the Devil's Course! Not even the king of hell himself could complete it!": "",
  "First titans and giants, now devils...? You sure pick some oddball names... But, I'm actually kind of intrigued.": "",
  "Excellent. Then come see me when you want to give the Devil's Course a shot. The price won't change any.": "",
  "I'll do that.": "",
  "Think you're tough enough to tackle the Devil's Course? Then hand over 300 yen and pick which version you want.": "",
  "Hm? Looks like you don't have enough on you.": "",
  "Well then. Knock 'em out the park... and into the next life.": "",
  "Is that right? Then come back whenever you feel up to the challenge.": "",
  "So you made it through the Home Run Hell, huh? ...Why haven't you gone pro?": "",
  "Well, I'm sure it's a whole different ballgame when you play against actual people.": "",
  "I'm sure you'd go pretty far! Either way, swing by again soon.": "",
  "Very impressive! Just as I expected outta you. Hope to see you around more often.": "",
  "Whoa! Can't believe you conquered the Chaotic Challenge... So when are you joining the big leagues?": "",
  "I think I'd rather stay a detective.": "",
  "Well, you sure are pro material. But to each his own. Hope to see you around.": "",
  "I guess even the likes of you would have trouble with it, huh? Well, come back and try again soon.": "",
  "Name's Yoshida, and I'm the manager of this here Batting Center. Pleased to meet ya.": "",
  "Oh, it's you, sir... Thank you for stopping by...": "",
  "Hey, what's going on? You look pretty wiped out.": "",
  "Oh, my apologies. It's just that lately we've had our fair share of... tiresome customers, you could say.": "",
  "Tiresome customers?": "",
  "Ah, I apologize. I'm sure you don't want to hear me griping...": "",
  "Actually, I wouldn't mind hearing you out.": "",
  "Very well then... I was about to say that I've been dealing with people who don't have the slightest idea how to order.": "",
  "Tell me, what do you think is the most troublesome kind of customer for a bartender?": "",
  "Huh, now there's a question...": "",
  "Oh no, there are in fact some people who don't care much for alcohol.": "",
  "Our job is to make it enjoyable even for customers like that, so that's not really an issue.": "",
  "I see. So what would you say is the real problem?": "",
  "Customers who only order the cheap stuff?": "",
  "Haha, the price is actually less of an issue. Our job is to simply provide the beverages our customers wish to drink.": "",
  "Customers who order cocktails that are a pain in the ass to make?": "",
  "That's actually when I get to show off my skills, so I prefer challenging situations like that.": "",
  "Hmm... I'm running out of ideas here...": "",
  "Customers who leave the order up to you?": "",
  "Precisely!": "",
  "A lot of customers think they're being savvy by ordering \"whatever I recommend,\" but in truth, it throws me off.": "",
  "Although I'm confident in each and every item on our menu, I have no idea how to tell what the customer really wants.": "",
  "Seeing as I'm not a mind-reader, I simply don't know what to make for them.": "",
  "I can see how that might end up giving you a headache. For instance, what if the customer refuses to drink it?": "",
  "That, or it might not suit their taste. That's why I'd appreciate a little more information on orders like those.": "",
  "I see. I guess it's better to put a little more effort into getting to know the bartender, huh?": "",
  "Indeed. It's different for regular customers, since I already know their preferences.": "",
  "Then I'd better stop by more often so you know what to get for me.": "",
  "Ah, please do! Would you like me to get something started?": "",
  "Geez, why couldn't he just make the damn drink?": "",
  "I know, right? I heard this was one of the oldest existing bars in Kamurocho, too. Guess we expected too much, babe.": "",
  "Ugh, what they did was \"set the bar\" too low! I wanna do something else!": "",
  "You wanna go bowling, then?": "",
  "Hmm... Fine, whatever, let's just go!": "",
  "(Looks like something went down at Bantam... Wonder what happened.)": "",
  "Hey there. Everything okay, chief?": "",
  "*sigh* Just another tiresome customer.": "",
  "Did they leave their order up to you again?": "",
  "No, this time they ordered a cocktail.": "",
  "And that's a problem?": "",
  "Well, it can be. Care to take a guess as to why?": "",
  "(A troublesome cocktail, huh... What could that be?)": "",
  "A cocktail that's a real hassle to make?": "",
  "Oh no. I'll craft any standard cocktail there is in no time flat.": "",
  "Okay, then...": "",
  "You didn't have the right ingredients?": "",
  "Our selection is the best in Kamurocho. We've never encountered such a thing.": "",
  "So that's not it. I wonder what it is...": "",
  "They ordered a cocktail you didn't know how to make?": "",
  "Even if I didn't know to make it, I would look it up in a cocktail book and whip up a bona fide masterpiece.": "",
  "They tried to order an original cocktail\nfrom a different bar?": "",
  "Precisely.": "",
  "The problem is, if another bar invented it, it's not\nexactly in my wheelhouse, you know?": "",
  "Seriously. How would you even know how to make it?": "",
  "When I first got the order, I looked it up in the back room because I'd never heard of it before...": "",
  "I couldn't find it at all, so then I asked the customer. And wouldn't you know it, they told me it was from another bar.": "",
  "I at least wanted to try to make it, so I asked them for the recipe. But they had no idea whatsoever.": "",
  "...Yeesh, what a waste.": "",
  "Unfortunately, at that point, there was nothing I could do.": "",
  "I understand. It should be common sense to not do something like that.": "",
  "Haha, well I'm glad you think so.": "",
  "By the way, does Bantam have their own original drink?": "",
  "We actually do not, but would you like me to prepare one on your behalf?": "",
  "Yes, I'll make it especially for you since I see you around so often. All you need to do is say the word.": "",
  "Hey, do you have a minute?": "",
  "Oh, were you talking to me?": "",
  "Yeah. I'm Sebastian Hutton...": "",
  "Also known as the world champion of drone racing!": "",
  "Whoa, the world champ, huh... What brings you to Kamurocho?": "",
  "Why, my sweet honey pie, of course! She lives here.": "",
  "Sweet honey— Oh, you mean your girlfriend. She's Japanese?": "",
  "Yep. Thanks to her, I'm fluent in the language now.": "",
  "I see. So, did you have some kind of business with me, or...": "",
  "Well, I heard they were holding a great big drone race here in Kamurocho, so I came to check it out.": "",
  "And every racer I've seen so far is nothing short of incredible... Particularly yourself!": "",
  "So I was hoping we could talk for a bit. Mind if I got your name?": "",
  "Takayuki Yagami... Okay, then I'm gonna call you \"Taka\"!": "",
  "Taka, you're practically a demon at drone racing!": "",
  "Thanks. That means a lot coming from the world champion.": "",
  "But I must say, your parts aren't really that good. You should consider upgrading.": "",
  "Is that right? I mean, you are the world champ, so... it makes perfect sense that my parts would pale in comparison.": "",
  "Then why don't I give you the inside scoop on how to build the best machine possible? I'm talking the parts I use.": "",
  "Really? You'd do that?": "",
  "Of course! A superb racer like you should use a machine that matches his skill.": "",
  "Wow... I'll be using a world-class drone, personally recommended by the world champ himself.": "",
  "However, I'll help you on one condition. I've devised a... test, of sorts, to see if you're worthy of using my build.": "",
  "What kind of test?": "",
  "Well, I've hidden specific \"build codes\" all across the city...": "",
  "And you'll be using your drone to find 'em.": "",
  "I see. Kind of like a scavenger hunt.": "",
  "Yes, all you need to do is fly your drone around and take pictures of whatever build codes you find.": "",
  "Sounds easy enough.": "",
  "That's right. Oh yeah, and there's a total of ten build codes per part.": "",
  "Come talk to me when you find ten codes for a given part. Then I'll give you the rundown on how to build it.": "",
  "Got it. As soon as I complete a build code, you'll be the first to know.": "",
  "Great! Good luck out there, Taka!": "",
  "(Not everyone gets to fly like the world champion of drones...)": "",
  "(Time for liftoff... Build codes, here I come!)": "",
  "Good job, Taka!": "",
  "I'm impressed you got all the frame codes.": "",
  "As promised, I'll give you all the deets on how to build the new parts.": "",
  "I appreciate that, Hutton-san.": "",
  "You bet!": "",
  "I'm impressed you got all the motor codes.": "",
  "I'm impressed you got all the propeller codes.": "",
  "I'm impressed you got all the turbo codes.": "",
  "I'm impressed you got all the ESC codes.": "",
  "Hey, Taka! Happy hunting so far? I can tell you how many build codes are still out there, if you'd like.": "",
  "As for frames, you have... <color=red>10</color> more codes to go.": "",
  "As for frames, you have... <color=red>9</color> more codes to go.": "",
